## 2026-09-23 — Checkpoint 03D runtime reduction

The initial 03D full grid was too expensive for 138 labeled parcels: CatBoost outer
fits were taking about 15 minutes each because every outer fold contained a
9-candidate x 3-inner-fold search plus refit. The default 03D config is now a
balanced-compute benchmark:

- preserve both frozen 5-fold outer protocols;
- preserve 3-fold inner CV;
- use 3 representative candidates for CatBoost, XGBoost, LightGBM, ExtraTrees,
  and HistGB instead of the wider 6-9 candidate grids;
- cap boosted models at 2500 estimators/iterations;
- reduce ExtraTrees from 3000 to 1500 trees.

This reduces inner/refit count from roughly 5570 fits to roughly 2540 before
accounting for shorter individual fits. The statistical evaluation structure is
unchanged; the reduction is in redundant hyperparameter tuning.

Important: partial results from the former wide grid must NOT be resumed into the
balanced grid. The runner now fingerprints the config/model/representation/compute
selection in _partial_state.json. A mismatch aborts --resume. Starting once
without --resume clears stale partials; subsequent interruptions can safely use
--resume.


## 2026-09-24 — Checkpoint 03D completed

Balanced 03D completed in 248.085 minutes with 230 outer fits and 6,348 OOF
rows across 23 eligible pairs. The robust finalists were all G1 agronomic:
HistGBLarge (state/grouped 0.549924/0.715339), XGBoostLarge
(0.525847/0.733080) and LightGBMLarge (0.540812/0.748478).

The result improves grouped global robustness relative to the frozen 03C
frontier but does not dominate both protocols. Broad global tuning is closed.

HistGB rank 1 was not ONNX-convertible under the stable stack. XGBoost rank 2
was the highest-ranked deployable finalist and its ONNX round trip passed with
maximum absolute difference 3.814697e-06. The global ONNX artifact is not
Local04D.

Do not compare state/grouped 03D RMSE directly with Local04D's target-matched
0.487845 as though they came from the same validation protocol.


## 2026-10-03 — Checkpoint 06 tail/regime plan opened

A teammate reported a possible residual pattern: Local04D and CatBoost appear to
predict most parcels well but miss a small number of very low- and high-yield
parcels. Because RMSE squares errors, a small extreme subset could dominate the
remaining objective.

This is not yet established. Checkpoint 06 was opened specifically to test the
claim before modeling it.

Canonical plan: `docs/CHECKPOINT_06_PLAN.md`.

The plan requires tail/SSE diagnostics, fold-valid tail definitions,
Local-vs-CatBoost error-overlap analysis, feature-family/variable importance,
tail/error-risk prediction from X, low-capacity calibration, conditional X-only
clustering and partially pooled regime correction. Promotion requires target-
matched development, LOSO and a new fresh confirmation bank.

No 06 model/result exists yet and no final prediction changed.
